  "_about": "Gear for chapter 1. The parts of him to wear gear on are Robin's (2026-11-20: 'We need slots for trinkets also. Two trinkets. I think we can skip rings. Do: Head, chest, legs, boots, necklace, two trinkets.'), with the cutlass and the buckler he picked earlier: nine places. `slots` are the places; a piece's own `slot` is its kind, and a trinket (kind `trinket`) goes in either of the two trinket places. A hat is what he wears on his head, a coat on his chest (the ids are older than Robin's words). What each kind gives is Victor, GD's: breeches and boots add health, a necklace adds to his swing, a trinket a little of both. Cutlass, buckler and hat show on him (Robin, 2026-11-20, 'The big pieces'); the rest show on his sheet. Three tiers, four rarities. A piece is a base and a rarity; its numbers are the base's times the rarity's `times`, and never less than the base plus one for each step of rarity. Affixes, uniques and sets are chapter 2. `value` is what a common one is worth; the shop sells at value times `buyTimes` and buys at value times `sellShare`. Names are Victor, GD's placeholders.",
